 field neither on the node nor given, a TypeError."] [349 1 "// astReduce is ast_type_reduce: (class, a None per field the node has up to the first it lacks, __dict__)."] [384 1 "// astRepr is ast_repr_max_depth (3.14): Name(...) past the depth, Name() without fields, else each field's"] [385 1 "// value, a list's or tuple's by astReprList, a node's one level deeper."] [431 1 "// astReprList is ast_repr_list: [] as repr, else the first and the last item (\"...\" between when more), a node one"] [432 1 "// level deeper."] [480 1 "// astSignature is a constructor's or product's __doc__ (asdl_c.py): NAME(TYPE[?*] FIELD, ...), NAME without fields;"] [481 1 "// Python.asdl's two \"expr?*\" sequences (Dict's keys, arguments' kw_defaults) as written there."] [529 2 "// AST's methods bind to the instance as method descriptors (methodDescrs; queue 202c: super().__init__ of a node"] [530 2 "// class's subclass, node.__replace__)"] [548 24 "// each node class's fields, for _field_types once every class exists"] [565 28 "// an optional attribute's default, at class level as CPython's"] [605 27 "// an optional field's default, at class level"] [626 2 "// a sum's __doc__ (asdl_c.py's visitSum): \"name = C1 | C2\" for a simple one, else one constructor a line"] [634 2 "// _field_types (CPython's add_ast_annotations: ast.dump reads it): a field's type, list[T] for a sequence, T | None"] [635 2 "// for an optional one (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 26] [96 32] [99 26] [131 37] [140 27] [150 128] [155 56] [179 79] [189 41] [198 36] [203 79] [225 23] [269 24] [290 24] [299 50] [301 33] [303 24] [337 37] [413 31] [419 23] [446 30] [648 26]]} (go/file "builtins_ast.go" :imports [


